# Gitignored local artifacts. Docker does not read .gitignore, so every one of
# these would otherwise be tarred up and shipped to the daemon by `COPY . .`,
# and would land in a builder-stage layer and the build cache.
#
# This list mirrors `.gitleaks.toml`'s allowlist on purpose: both files are
# answering the same question — which gitignored local artifacts are here and
# what is in them — and they had drifted. `certificates/` holds a dev TLS
# *private key*, which is why gitleaks allowlists it; `.worktrees/` is other
# checkouts of this repo and had grown to several gigabytes, so the build
# context was that big before the first instruction ran.
.worktrees
.claude/worktrees
certificates
data
playwright-report
# fnox.toml holds the NAME of every secret this project uses, as references
# rather than values, so this is not a leak and multi-stage means it never
# reached the published image anyway. It belongs here for the same reason
# `certificates/` and `data/` do: it is a gitignored local artifact, and the
# build context is not the place for one. Deliberately NOT added to
# .gitleaks.toml, despite the mirroring note above — a reference file should
# stay scanned, precisely so a real value pasted into it gets caught.
fnox.toml

# Development-only trees the runtime image has no use for.
# `playwright.config.ts` goes with e2e-tests, not merely alongside it: it sits
# at the root, tsconfig includes `**/*.ts`, and it imports ./e2e-tests/env — so
# dropping the tests without it fails `next build` at the type-check step.
.claude
.github
.kamal
e2e-tests
playwright.config.ts
plans

# Test files, for the same reason and one step further. `tsconfig.json`
# includes `**/*.ts`, so `next build` type-checks every test left in the
# context — and a test importing something excluded above fails the *image*
# build with no local symptom at all, because the file resolves fine in the
# checkout. That has now happened twice: first `playwright.config.ts`
# importing ./e2e-tests/env, and then `src/lib/server/audioSweep.test.ts`
# importing ../../../e2e-tests/fake-s3.js to borrow a real HTTP bucket.
#
# Naming each casualty is whack-a-mole, so the tests go instead. The runtime
# image has no use for one, and nothing outside a test imports `testSupport`
# (checked, not assumed).
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
src/lib/testSupport

# Documentation
README.md
LICENCE
docs
